{
  "id": "grammar.a1.hobbies.02.regular-present",
  "title": "Regular present-tense hobby verbs",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Describe hobbies",
      "content": "Use familiar regular present-tense verbs to say what you do in your free time."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Common hobby verbs",
      "rows": [
        [
          "Estudio.",
          "I study."
        ],
        [
          "Trabajo.",
          "I work."
        ],
        [
          "Bailo.",
          "I dance."
        ],
        [
          "Camino.",
          "I walk."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "examples",
      "items": [
        {
          "spanish": "Bailo los viernes.",
          "english": "I dance on Fridays."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Camino en el parque.",
          "english": "I walk in the park."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Estudio español.",
          "english": "I study Spanish."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "tip",
      "content": "You know from Unit 7 that the ending changes with the person: *bailo*, *bailas*, *baila*. In this lesson you use the *yo* form to say what you do."
    }
  ]
}
